WEBVTT

00:00:10.790 --> 00:00:12.200
I wonder who that is?

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.620
He's super hot!

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:14.830
What is he doing here?

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:17.370
What's going on?

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.700
There's a commotion amongst the girls some reason...

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.700
If you're looking for her, she's in her extra classes.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.290
I'm here because I have some business with you.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.120
I'm pretty surprised you're wearing those broken glasses.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.620
What kind of intelligence are you working with here?

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.700
You're the one that did this!

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.500
Don't you have spare pair?

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.500
No.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.620
My dead grandmother bought these for me,
so I only use these and I take care of them.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:53.250
Uh...

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.290
Huh? H-hey!

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.750
What the...?

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.000
Ichiban daijin a koto wa
The most important thing

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:07.120
Daremo shiranai koto nanda
Is something nobody knows

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:11.200
Are mo kore mo daijina you de
Things which may be considered important

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.750
Toki ga sugireba kiete yuku
May fade away as time goes by

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:22.540
Kaze ni notte kumo no kirema ni
Romance in pale pink

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:28.910
Tadayou no wa omoide no you na
Like the palm of a hand which has begun to color

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:38.250
Irozuki hajimeta te no hira no you na
Riding on the wind

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:44.950
Usubeni iro no koigokoro
Just like memories drifting in the break in the clouds

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.290
Toki wo kakenuke yagate kuru
The new season will come soon

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:56.250
Atarashii kisetsu yume to wa sukoshi chigau
Leaping through time

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.750
Tada oboeteiru koto wa
And it's little different from a dream

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:05.660
Daijina koto nanda
But the things I remember are very important

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:11.370
Ichiban daijina kotoba
The most important words

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:15.450
Daremo iwazuni owarisou
May never be said to anybody

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.410
Are mo kore mo daijoubu sa
Everything will be all right

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.370
Toki ga sugitemo oboeteru
Even though time passes, I will remember

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:27.290
Anata no koto wa oboeteru
I will remember you

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.290
About the Shape of Out Love.

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:39.980
Nishiyama Glasses

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.540
Uh... Thanks.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:48.580
Well... He is her brother, so he can't be a bad person.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:53.870
For all I know, I'm just the type that he hates the most.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.330
I don't like this! You're lookin' at me scary!

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.250
Hurry and get to the point.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:14.790
The more I look at you, the more unappealing you are.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.950
I wonder why Iroha is dating a guy like you.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.410
I'm asking about what you want, though.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:25.290
Yesterday, I tried asking Iroha what it is
that she likes about you.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.950
Wh-what did she say?

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:27.620
Everything.

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:30.250
What?! I don't think that's true, though...

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.040
I thought the same thing, so I asked her more.

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.120
How long have you been dating him?

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.830
Uh, about two months.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.540
Where do you always meet up?

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:44.290
At school or the park...

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.660
Iroha, your birthday was the other day, right?
What did he do for you?

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.200
He gave me a handmade figure.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:01.410
In my opinion, I don't think she'd seriously like a guy
that can only manage this childish relationship.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:05.000
I'll tell you one thing, Iroha is being raised well.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:11.660
A mediocre guy like you acting like her boyfriend,
is really unpleasant as her family.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.160
If this is a meaningless relationship,
then I want you to end it.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.120
That's all I came to say.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.910
What is a relationship with meaning, then?

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.080
Has our entire relationship up until now had no meaning?

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.870
No, that isn't right...

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:50.410
Even though I mean to cherish her,
it's somehow disappointing.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:52.330
But...

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.250
It's true that I'm mediocre.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:58.950
And it's also true that I can't do anything for her.

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:15.200
Wh-what am I doing?!

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.330
This is just like a stalker!

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.540
I have to get out of here before she discovers me!

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.910
Ito-senp...

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:26.620
Morning, Ayado! Lovely weather today!

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.620
Yes, very nice! But I heard it will rain this evening.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.870
Please be careful on your way home.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.040
Right.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:38.250
Uh... Um, Ayado.

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:40.160
If you don't mind, let's go out aga-

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.290
Yeah, the picnic! It was fun, wasn't it?

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.580
I definitely want to go together with everyone again!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.080
Yeah... Let's all go together.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.660
Ultimately, I couldn't come up
with a way to resolve things.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.580
Ito and Ayado...

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.000
Could it be that... everything's okay?

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.870
How embarrassing...

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:22.000
We definitely don't have the type of relationship
where I can invite her out anytime, but...

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:26.540
What am I doing?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:31.700
What is it?

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.410
Getting a phone call from you is freaky.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.410
I want to ask you something! Don't get carried away!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.540
You're the only one I can talk to about this!

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.160
Oh? Well, I'd sure like to eat a parfait...

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:44.160
I'll treat you!

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.410
So you want to do something for Igarashi?

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.410
You should ask her about that.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.410
She probably wouldn't tell me.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.000
Then I think you should give her a ring or something.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.410
A ring?

00:06:57.410 --> 00:07:01.410
Isn't that kind of simple?
Are you even thinking before you talk?

00:07:01.410 --> 00:07:02.700
That's rude!

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:07.000
You want to give her something, right?!
You want to improve the feelings of romance, right?!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:11.660
A ring strengthens the feeling that she's yours,
and Igarashi would definitely appreciate it!

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:14.040
And you'll look all lovey-dovey
to the people around you too!

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:17.000
No matter what my boyfriend accomplishes,
I'm what he wants the most!

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.910
Oh, MAN, I really want a boyfriend!

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:24.370
Oh! I see... Makes sense.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.950
I can make it happen if I sell
the anime and games I have at home.

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:30.120
That isn't happy at all...

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:33.620
Work! My uncle is looking
for some part-timers for an amusement park!

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.370
O-okay. Thank you for everything.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:43.370
Yeah. Excuse me! One more parfait!

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:55.000
What in the world does Ishino's uncle do?

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.830
Mr. Bunny! Can we take a picture together?

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.290
Yeah!

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.410
Yay! It's a bunny!

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.200
What is this sense of omnipotence?

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.200
So cute!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:05.660
What is this sense of omnipotence?

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:06.870
What is this sense of omnipotence?

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:06.870
Okay, I'm taking the picture!

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:07.910
Okay, I'm taking the picture!

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.120
It's fun!

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:19.700
This might actually be work out.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:23.660
I came to the amusement park with her...

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:28.200
And that gift gave her so much joy.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.750
Thank you. I'm really happy.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:36.370
I will always absolutely cherish this.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:41.700
To see
that smile,
I'll do
my best

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:40.790
To see that smile, I'll do my best.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.080
Tsutsun. Let's go home together.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.410
Uh, sorry, we can't go home together today.

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:51.250
Huh?

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:58.290
We might not be able
to go home together tomorrow either.

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.700
Then when can we?

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.290
Uh...

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:03.330
If we can't walk home after school,
then can we meet on the weekend?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:10.000
Your brother still doesn't really like me, huh?

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:14.370
It's fine, just ignore him. He's always been a worrywart.

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:19.330
If you were my sibling,
I think I'd probably be worried, too.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:21.200
Tsutsun...

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.830
So, see you later.

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.080
Huh? Igarashi!

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.660
Something wrong? You're just standing there.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.910
Nope, it's nothing.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:43.790
Hey, wanna go eat ramen with us?

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:45.410
We found a good shop.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.700
And Takanashi says he'll pay!

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:49.000
Except, I didn't say that.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.040
I think I'll head home for today.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.370
How much more until my goal...?

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:05.160
I wonder if they'll give me more time
after school and not just on the weekends.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.120
Tsutsun.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:25.660
He's been busy lately. I wonder what he's doing.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.330
They're thin...

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:14.700
Hey, Mewgarl.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.250
Maybe she's on a walk today.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:30.620
You've been coming home early lately.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:34.160
Tsutsun hasn't been able to walk home with me recently.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:34.950
Why not?

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.330
No idea.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:38.000
Why don't you ask him?

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:41.120
I don't need to... I trust him.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.080
So it's finally gotten to that, huh?

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:45.660
What has?

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:50.540
The other day I met with him and I said something.
I told him to break up with you.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:53.160
That's probably why he's chickening ou-

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.660
Why would you do that?

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:58.000
We're not going to break up.

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:00.660
He's actually just putting distance
between you two, right?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.250
So this is how far it's gotten.

00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:05.750
There are so many better guys for you out the-

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.700
There's no one better than Tsutsun!

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:20.200
Why are you so agitated?

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:26.080
Chika. In a family, there are things that are okay
and things that are not okay for a brother to do.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.080
I'm not your brother...

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:32.660
...since, you know...

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.830
...we aren't blood-related.

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:41.000
You know, we aren't blood-related.

00:12:41.660 --> 00:12:42.750
That's true...

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:47.750
but we've been together since age 5,
so there's no reason to even bring that up right now.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:55.450
Then I hope it goes as well as possible,

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.620
if you really trust him that much.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.040
Send it back!
Pass! Pass it!

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.500
I'm passing it to you!

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.250
Okay!

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:06.080
Okay!

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:12.950
I haven't really been able to sleep lately, so I'm drowsy.

00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:21.700
A Mewgon has appeared
Fight
Magic
Guard
Run

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:17.200
I thought about it but I can't come up with anything,

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:20.700
so in the end it's best not to do anything.

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:24.700
I'm okay with it.

00:13:26.540 --> 00:13:29.040
If this will be settled by holding back my feelings...

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:30.370
You're just entirely useless, huh?

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.200
You're just entirely useless, huh?

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.200
If it will make everything go as well as it has been...

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.830
If it will make everything go as well as it has been...

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.830
But how?!

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.870
Isn't that for your sake and not for others?

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.620
Since you don't like saying
how you really feel and causing conflict,

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:45.120
you won't change because
you don't want to get hurt, right?

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:48.620
Watch out!

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:49.370
Huh?

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.080
You hit Cat Ears!

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:54.250
Are you okay?!

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.000
Why're you all spaced?

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.040
Were you watchin' anime all night?

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:14.330
Get it together, Cat Ears!

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:21.500
What am I even laughing at?

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:24.500
Oh, there you are!

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.290
Igarashi, why are you here?

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:31.000
I saw you fall down earlier. Are you okay?

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.580
Yeah, I'm alright.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:46.750
When we went camping, there was something
you were worried about, right?

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:49.700
Are you still worried about that now?

00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:53.080
Yeah... I suppose so.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:57.120
I see... I'm useless, aren't I?

00:14:58.410 --> 00:15:01.120
Why are you feeling down, Igarashi?

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:06.250
Because I was only thinking about myself,
and I didn't notice anything about you...

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.540
Even though we were together the whole time... Sorry.

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.750
Somehow... you've become like Tsutsui.

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:15.910
Huh?

00:15:16.870 --> 00:15:21.580
How you can properly put what you're thinking
into words and then confront someone.

00:15:22.450 --> 00:15:29.540
The other day, Tsutsui said "I'm so happy
you came to like a girl," and "I want you to be happy..."

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.330
I was a bit embarrassed.

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.750
But I was happy about that.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:41.910
Well, for me, Tsutsun is the first person
that I've honestly fallen for.

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.450
Is that so?

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:47.580
If you like someone, there will be lots of things
that you'll want them to understand,

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:53.370
and as someone important to you, you'll clash,
but even if it's hard you have to express it to them.

00:15:58.080 --> 00:16:03.410
Before... I met Tsutsui, I couldn't show
that to the people important to me.

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:06.620
I thought it would be better than having a conflict.

00:16:07.410 --> 00:16:15.290
But, since my stifled emotions aren't able
to go anywhere, they end up staying inside of me.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:22.790
Igarashi... please, don't laugh.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:25.620
I think...

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.000
...you're also one of my most important friends!

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:37.040
Properly saying that is embarrassing...

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:38.830
Yeah.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:42.870
But you're happy after all, right?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:46.080
Yeah.

00:16:48.160 --> 00:16:51.370
Thank you, Ito. You gave me courage.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:16:59.620
Tsutsun.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.250
What's up?

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.830
What have you been doing after school lately?

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:14.370
Tell me why we can't walk home together.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:16.950
Huh? Uh...

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:22.660
I'm scared, but if you don't put it into words,
it won't get through to me.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.120
Wait a second. I'm going to explain right now.

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:28.540
I don't know what Chika said to you, but...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.160
I...

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:33.200
don't want to break up.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.000
Of course.

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:42.700
Sorry. I wanted to work more
and buy you something better,

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:46.750
but I found out your ring size
and I got into such a mood that...

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:52.040
I wanted to get it early and I bought it.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:15.750
I can't explain to anyone what there is between us,

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:19.250
but I won't let them say that it's meaningless.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:26.380
This girl
changed my

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:26.380
entire world

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:25.370
This girl changed my entire world.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:31.370
And there's Ito who dealt with both me and Ayado
and his complicated feelings.

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:37.830
And Ishino, who gave me advice,
and Takanashi who liked Iroha at one point,

00:18:38.410 --> 00:18:41.370
and Ayado who fell in love with me.

00:18:42.290 --> 00:18:47.620
For the sake of all of those people,
the meaning is surely that she must be happy.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:52.500
For now, this is all I could do.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.080
Thank you, Tsutsun.

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:01.450
I never want to forget this day.

00:19:33.620 --> 00:19:34.870
Iroha...

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:58.750
Yume ga same sora nagamete omou
I wake from a dream and gaze at the sky

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:04.080
Mune wo utsu ano kotoba kirei da
And think of those beautiful words that touched my heart

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:08.450
Uwabe kazarazu hanasetara na...
If only I could talk to you without putting on airs...

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:13.910
Sobietatsu fuan no tou ga
Is the pillar of fear towering above it all

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:18.290
Ari no mama de ii no kana??
Okay just the way it is?

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:23.540
Nan oku kounen nayameba ii no darou??
For how many millions of light-years must I suffer??

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:26.700
Saa sugu doa akete
Come on, open the door now

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:28.790
Ai ni yukou
And let's meet

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:33.750
Imi nado nai yo hotondo ga
Most of it means nothing, you know

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:38.250
Kimi ni sokkou de minukareru no osorete
The fear that you immediately see through me

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:43.450
Koukai bakari da ne futari wa kitto
Fills me with regret, surely

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:48.500
Zutto miageteta sora wa sotto
The sky that we always stared up at, quietly

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:53.370
Bokura no asu wo terasu kitto
It will brighten our tomorrow, surely

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.500
Kimi ni aitai desu
I want to see you

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:58.000
Sugoku kantan na koto nan jan ne
That's not a super easy thing, right?

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.750
Hora mijukumono
Hey, the inexperienced

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:04.500
Seishun believer desu
Are believers in youth.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:12.900
INFERNO RAMEN

00:21:10.950 --> 00:21:12.870
Can I take your order?

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.870
One pork broth soy ramen.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.290
One pork broth, very firm noodles.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.660
Wonton noodles.

00:21:17.790 --> 00:21:21.000
Miso ramen with extra spring onion,
and a half-order of fried rice.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.620
I'll have Mazesoba.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:22:50.900
INFERNO RAMEN

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.830
Here's your order.

00:21:25.000 --> 00:21:27.290
Let's eat!

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:31.040
Yum.

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:32.410
This is good.

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:37.450
I didn't know there was such
a delicious ramen shop here.

00:21:37.580 --> 00:21:41.290
Right? The wood carving of the bear
gives a great atmosphere too.

00:21:41.660 --> 00:21:44.120
Okay, here's your half-order of fried rice.

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:45.660
This half order is huge...

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:50.660
By the way, it feels like Ishino found this one,
but I'm the one that found this place.

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:54.290
Takanashi, I'm impressed by your
investigative spirit concerning ramen.

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.450
There's a part of you that speaks to otaku, huh?

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:58.620
Ishino, careful with the spring onion.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:02.410
Eek! Takanashi, you're worried about me!
Are we gonna date?

00:22:02.410 --> 00:22:03.500
We will not.

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:09.160
I feel like I'm forgetting something.

00:22:09.580 --> 00:22:12.250
Huh?! What is it, Tsutsui?

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:15.290
This was the special memorial event for
the opening date of theatrical version of Ezomichi!

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:18.160
This is not the time to pretend
to be imitating normies at this place!

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:20.040
Let's hurry up and eat and go home, Tsutsui!

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:20.540
Yeah!

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:24.160
Do you guys think you can go home
immediately after eating ramen?

00:22:24.160 --> 00:22:24.910
Huh?!

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:29.160
When you eat something salty,
you start wanting something sweet, right, Igarashi?

00:22:29.160 --> 00:22:31.580
I want to eat a chocolate parfait.

00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:34.410
Ooh! Well then, wanna go to a family diner?

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:35.950
It'll be Tsutsui's treat.

00:22:35.950 --> 00:22:36.950
H-hey!

00:22:36.950 --> 00:22:40.540
Dude, how much do you think
I've been watching out for you, huh?

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:42.500
Oh, Tsutsui's paying...
Gonna go eat somewhere else?
Huh? You're right...

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:43.410
No, it's okay. It's fine. I've got this!

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:44.250
Let's get going!

00:22:43.410 --> 00:22:44.250
No, it's okay. It's fine. I've got this!

00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:44.870
No, it's okay. It's fine. I've got this!

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:46.120
On to the next spot!

00:22:46.620 --> 00:22:48.620
It's okay! It's really okay! Thanks for the meal...!

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:50.410
Thanks for the meal!
